 "_arm_note": {
  "arm": "F1_t9_fullft",
  "changes": {
   "use_lora": false
  },
  "why": "the paper table's 'SCA, full finetuning' control at the SAME configuration as the reported row. The only prior full-FT arms (x1_xenc_full*) predate query weighting AND carried the double-parameterized cross-encoder, so their numbers (MSR-VTT 45.7) are retracted and nothing clean exists to fill that row.",
  "baseline": "config/sca/ablations/T9_qweight_only.json",
  "expectation": "full-FT also trains the cross-encoder with the retrieval loss -- the drift X3-X5 measured at 51.4/51.1/50.9 against 54.8 frozen -- so this row is expected BELOW the LoRA row; that contrast is the point of it."
 }
}
